        "topicId": "math-y9-simultaneous-equations",
        "stem": "A shop sells identical packs A and B. Two A and three B cost £7; six A and nine B cost £21. A second supplier offers the same items, and two A plus three B cost £7 but six A plus nine B cost £20. A third supplier quotes two A plus three B for £7 and four A plus five B for £12. Which option correctly describes the number of possible real unit-price pairs at suppliers 1, 2, 3 respectively, and gives the third supplier's B price?",
