        "topicId": "math-y9-simultaneous-equations",
        "stem": "A pupil is given $3x+2y=17$ and $5x-2y=7$. Instead of copying these equations, she writes their sum and twice their difference (first minus second). Another pupil writes twice their sum and four times their difference. Which pair gives the common solution (x,y) and the value of the second pupil's difference-equation right-hand side?",
